### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3001
@oauthServer = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### 2. Get Application Info
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/info

### 3. Home Page (Check Auth Status)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/auth/oauth/authorize?response_type=code&client_id=4xsmjvVypydAOUFZrDxwn12J-rWdFIYa&redirect_uri=http://localhost:3001/callback&scope=read&state=test123


### 4. Start OAuth2 Login Flow
# This will redirect to OAuth2 server authorization page
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/login

### 5. OAuth2 Callback (Manual Test)
# Note: This endpoint is normally called by OAuth2 server after user authorization
# You need to get the 'code' and 'state' from the actual OAuth flow
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/callback?code=AUTHORIZATION_CODE_HERE&state=STATE_VALUE_HERE

### 6. Get User Profile (Protected - requires authentication)
# Note: You need to be logged in first via browser flow
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/profile
Cookie: connect.sid=SESSION_COOKIE_HERE

### 7. Access Protected Resource (Protected - requires authentication)
# Note: You need to be logged in first via browser flow
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/protected
Cookie: connect.sid=SESSION_COOKIE_HERE

### 8. Logout
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Cookie: connect.sid=SESSION_COOKIE_HERE

###############################################
### Browser-based Flow Test Instructions
###############################################

### Step 1: Start Login Flow
# Open browser and go to: http://localhost:3001/auth/login
# This will redirect you to OAuth2 server

### Step 2: Login at OAuth2 Server
# Login with credentials:
# Username: admin@example.com
# Password: password123

### Step 3: Get Session Cookie
# After successful login, check browser dev tools > Application > Cookies
# Copy the 'connect.sid' cookie value

### Step 4: Test Protected Endpoints
# Use the session cookie in the requests above

###############################################
### Testing OAuth2 Server Integration
###############################################

### Check OAuth2 Server Health
GET {{oauthServer}}/health

### Get OAuth2 Server Endpoints
GET {{oauthServer}}/api/endpoints

### Get OIDC Discovery Document
GET {{oauthServer}}/api/auth/oauth/.well-known/openid-configuration

### OAuth2 Authorization URL (Manual Construction)
# GET {{oauthServer}}/api/auth/oauth/authorize?response_type=code&client_id=4xsmjvVypydAOUFZrDxwn12J-rWdFIYa&redirect_uri=http://localhost:3001/auth/callback&scope=openid%20profile%20email&state=RANDOM_STATE&nonce=RANDOM_NONCE

###############################################
### Direct Token Testing (for debugging)
###############################################

### Exchange Authorization Code for Token (Manual)
POST {{oauthServer}}/api/auth/oauth/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=authorization_code&code=AUTHORIZATION_CODE&redirect_uri=http://localhost:3001/auth/callback&client_id=4xsmjvVypydAOUFZrDxwn12J-rWdFIYa&client_secret=9mYxPS4p_G-LoxaYnT-szafwVoRwh_BLe9zh1TGcGBZgi0OJISppd4U12KK_2tsh

### Get User Info with Access Token
GET {{oauthServer}}/api/auth/oauth/userinfo
Authorization: Bearer ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

### Refresh Token
POST {{oauthServer}}/api/auth/oauth/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=refresh_token&refresh_token=REFRESH_TOKEN_HERE&client_id=4xsmjvVypydAOUFZrDxwn12J-rWdFIYa&client_secret=9mYxPS4p_G-LoxaYnT-szafwVoRwh_BLe9zh1TGcGBZgi0OJISppd4U12KK_2tsh

###############################################
### Complete Flow Test Script
###############################################

### Test 1: Application Status
GET {{baseUrl}}/
Accept: application/json

###
### Test 2: Login Redirect (will return HTML redirect)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Accept: text/html

###
### Test 3: Check OAuth Server Discovery
GET {{oauthServer}}/api/auth/oauth/.well-known/openid-configuration
Accept: application/json

###############################################
### Error Cases Testing
###############################################

### Test Invalid State Parameter
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/callback?code=test&state=invalid_state

### Test Missing Authorization Code
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/callback?state=valid_state

### Test Access Protected Without Auth
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/profile

### Test Access Protected Without Auth
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/protected

###############################################
### Curl Commands for Terminal Testing
###############################################

### Test with curl (copy these to terminal)

# Health check
# curl -i http://localhost:3001/health

# App info
# curl -i http://localhost:3001/api/info

# Start login (will show redirect)
# curl -i http://localhost:3001/auth/login

# Test protected endpoint (will fail without session)
# curl -i http://localhost:3001/api/profile

# Test with session cookie (replace SESSION_COOKIE with actual value)
# curl -i -H "Cookie: connect.sid=SESSION_COOKIE" http://localhost:3001/api/profile

###############################################
### Notes:
###############################################

# 1. The OAuth2 flow requires browser interaction for the authorization step
# 2. Session cookies are httpOnly and secure, so they need to be extracted from browser
# 3. For automated testing, consider implementing a test endpoint that bypasses OAuth
# 4. The authorization code is single-use and expires quickly
# 5. State parameter prevents CSRF attacks and must match between requests